-- =============================================================================
-- A multi-clause group is compiled to local definitions named
-- `__pm_fallthrough_<k>`, and a drafter can spell that name too. Here the
-- clauses after the first one can never run, so their binding is checked and
-- then dropped; the first clause's body still reads the drafter's own
-- `__pm_fallthrough_0`, and answers 7 (review of legalese/l4-ide#545; probe
-- h02). An earlier build let it read the dropped binding instead, and failed
-- with an internal error when it ran.
-- =============================================================================
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

`__pm_fallthrough_0` MEANS 7

GIVEN c IS A Colour
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `refs user` c   IS `__pm_fallthrough_0`
DECIDE `refs user` Red IS 2

#EVAL `refs user` Green -- 7
#EVAL `refs user` Red   -- 7: the first clause matches every input
